# Mechanism: pre-release-dialog-network-safety

command: python3 -B scripts/check-pre-release-external-input-safety.py XIS-001
inputs:
  - .cairn/mechanisms/pre-release-dialog-network-safety
  - Cargo.toml
  - Cargo.lock
  - src/core/owned_process.rs
  - src/widgets/dialog
  - tests/api_widget_behavior.rs
  - tests/api_widget_behavior/dialog_http.rs
  - tests/support/app_input.rs
  - scripts/check-pre-release-external-input-safety.py
  - scripts/check-dialog-http.py
  - manual/dialogs.md
  - docs/spec/pre-release-external-input-safety.md
  - docs/commitments/pre-release-external-input-safety.md
requirements:
  - XIS-001

The check MUST first prove its observation validator rejects a request process
that inherits an unrelated value, loses a supported proxy or certificate
setting, changes the fixed curl arguments, exposes the private request outside
stdin, skips a request, or starts curl while both public endpoint options are
disabled.

The check MUST then use a fake curl executable to record both the version probe
and request process. It MUST verify their arguments, private stdin, restricted
environment, response limit, deadline, cancellation, and cleanup. Public input
validation and autocomplete configurations with no endpoint MUST not start the
fake executable. Enabled configurations MUST reach the fake HTTP server only
after their documented trigger and must retain the existing protocol, response,
and ownership bounds. The dialog manual MUST name the network triggers, limits,
allowed protocols, required curl version, and forwarded environment groups.
